FAAD2 compatibility library
==========================

This package provides the legacy NeAACDec API and libfaad.so.2 ABI as a thin
shim over libfaad3. It builds only the library; the CLI ships with libfaad3.
Output channel order and positions follow FAAD2.

Build and install libfaad3 first (https://github.com/nschimme/faac, branch
libfaad, Meson option -Ddecoder=true). Then, with CMake and pkg-config installed:

    PKG_CONFIG_PATH=/path/to/libfaad3/lib/pkgconfig cmake -S . -B build
    cmake --build build
    cmake --install build

Use -DBUILD_SHARED_LIBS=OFF for a static library. Static consumers must also
link libfaad3; pkg-config --libs --static faad2 supplies the dependencies.

Main/LTP/SSR/LD/ER profiles, DRM, fixed-point decoding, LATM, ADIF, and raw AAC
without AudioSpecificConfig (ASC) are no longer supported. useOldADTSFormat
and dontUpSampleImplicitSBR are ignored. LC-only streams at or below 24 kHz
are reported at their real sample rate and are not upsampled to twice the
rate. The legacy InitDRM entry point remains exported but reports failure.

The output format and downMatrix setting are fixed when the decoder is
initialized (NeAACDecInit/NeAACDecInit2); a change made later applies at the
next NeAACDecPostSeekReset or NeAACDecInit.

Dynamic range control is applied as in FAAD2: full compression, and streams
that carry a programme reference level are normalised to -20 dBFS. Streams that
carry compression data but no programme reference level are not attenuated by
20 dB, which FAAD2 did.
